      "writtenOn": "2025-02-13T20:02:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe that the current exit() implementation will reboot only if there is only one thread running and the watchdog reset is called. If multiple threads are running, I believe, the Zephyr OS will move to other threads. I believe in the current implementation, even if we exit an essential thread, it will go to other threads (if there exists some) without triggerring reboot. I will defer to @patrykd@google.com and @dawidn@google.com to provide more detailed answers.",
      "parentUuid": "5c1ef44f_8f6f6433",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 44,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "db2ed5d2a7af7f20bc9f1d54e1cdc81e1a4c873d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
